/*
 * GENERATED by tools/coa_spec_header_bauen.py from mod-playerbots-coa.
 * Do not edit by hand - the next run overwrites it.
 *
 * One row per CoA specialization: which role it plays, where it stands, and
 * which rotation it runs. The source is the same one the rotations and the
 * seeded database rows come from, so core and database cannot drift apart.
 *
 * Why this lives in the core rather than in the database: AiFactory only knows
 * the nine base classes, and PlayerbotFactory::Randomize falls back to exactly
 * that point through ResetStrategies(). Seeded rows are gone after that, code
 * is not.
 *
 * The first row of a class is its default - the spec a bot gets when none has
 * been chosen yet.
 */

